WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.872
NARRATOR: What's more
thrilling than a shark?

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.607
A mob of them.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.477
Sharks might have
invented crowdsourcing.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:18.284
Every year between May and July,
billions of migrating sardines

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:25.392
come to spawn off the
coast of South Africa,

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.628
catering one of the largest
feeding frenzies in the world.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.168
Sharks make the guest list.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.303
Hundreds of copper
sharks swooping through

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.305
a dense oily cloud of fish.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.641
[music playing]

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.487
The sardines try to
thwart the attack

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:59.259
by banding together into a
tight shimmering disco ball.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:03.396
When a shark strikes, the
sardines scatter and escape,

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.898
or at least that's the plan.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.438
But the battle's not over.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.340
While the sharks harass
the sardines from below,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.611
cape gannets mount
an aerial attack.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.981
Sharks and birds corner
the little fishes,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.349
benefiting them both.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.255
[birds chirping]

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.528
Air trapped in their
feathers hampers

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.331
the gannets' ability
to dive deep,

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.933
so they have to strike hard.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.606
They hit the water head first
with arrow-like posture,

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.942
folding their wings
behind them to minimize

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.809
the force of impact.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:58.818
Besieged on all sides, the
sardine defense starts to fail.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.287
[music playing]

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:13.633
To make things worse, a Bryde's
whale crashes the party.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.904
Rising from the depths,
this 15 ton giant devours

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.706
sardines by the thousands.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.916
Even the copper sharks give this
50 foot behemoth a wide berth.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:47.367
And then it's over as
suddenly as it began.

